  "lineage": "Song tradition of the Tiwi people of Bathurst and Melville Islands, north of Darwin, whose singers fit new texts to inherited melodic forms for the kulama yam ceremony, for yoi dancing at pukumani mortuary ceremonies and for everyday events. The Tiwi Strong Women's Group, working with researcher Genevieve Campbell on returning archival recordings to the community, released Ngarukuruwala: We Sing Songs (Skinnyfish, 2010).",
